id: 13
hanzi: 主人
pinyin: zhǔ rén
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: host; master; owner; proprietor
  es: amo; anfitrión; dueño; propietario

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | an owner of property, pet, or estate; a person who employs servants/workers | amo; dueño; propietario; patrón | 房屋主人 (owner of the house)
  2 | Noun | Standard | host receiving guests | anfitrión que recibe a sus invitados | 热情的主人 (hospitable host)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 庄园主人见年轻的子路为人忠厚诚实、干活勤快，便决定将他留下来长期做工。 | Zhuāngyuán zhǔrén jiàn niánqīng de Zǐlù wéirén zhōnghòu chéngshí, gànhuó qínkuài, biàn juédìng jiāng tā liú xiàlái chángqī zuògōng. | Seeing that young Zilu was honest, dependable, and diligent in labor, the estate master decided to keep him for long-term work. | Viendo que el joven Zilu era honesto, leal y trabajador, el dueño de la hacienda decidió contratarlo de forma permanente.
  #2 | 作为本次国际青年创新论坛的东道主，主人以热忱周到的服务赢得了各国与会代表的一致赞誉。 | Zuòwéi běncì guójì qīngnián chuàngxīn lùntán de dōngdàozhǔ, zhǔrén yǐ rèchén zhōudào de fúwù yíngdé le gèguó yùhuì dàibiǎo de yízhì zànyù. | As host of this international youth innovation forum, the organizers won unanimous praise from multinational delegates for warm, attentive service. | Como anfitrión del foro internacional de innovación juvenil, el organizador se ganó el elogio unánime de los delegados extranjeros por su hospitalidad impecable.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  房屋主人 | owner of the house; landlord
  庄园主人 | master of the estate
  热情的主人 | hospitable host
  国家的主人 | masters of the nation
  宠物主人 | pet owner
  宴会主人 | banquet host

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  喧宾夺主 | xuān bīn duó zhǔ | the guest eclipses the host; the secondary supersedes the primary
  反客为主 | fǎn kè wéi zhǔ | turn from guest into host; take the initiative
  做家作主 | zuò jiā zuò zhǔ | run the household and take charge
  主客尽欢 | zhǔ kè jìn huān | both host and guests thoroughly enjoy themselves

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  主 | zhǔ | master; host; primary | amo; anfitrión; principal | 丶 | dot / flame | 丶 (lamp flame / sacred spark) | 王/土 (lampstand base) | 5 | 单一结构 | Pictographic depiction of an oil lamp with flame burning steadily on a stand, symbolizing the head of household presiding over sacred fires. | A sacred flame burning atop an altar lampstand, representing authority and leadership. | Una llama sagrada que arde sobre un candelabro, símbolo de autoridad y primacía doméstica. | 214 | YG | ""
  人 | rén | person; human | persona; ser humano | 人 | human | 丿 (left falling torso) | ㇏ (right stepping leg) | 2 | 单一结构 | Pictograph of a human standing with legs apart, representing humanity. | A human walking forward with two supporting legs. | Un ser humano caminando con paso firme sobre dos piernas. | 35 | O | ""

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: The person (人) holding primary authority like a steady flame atop a lampstand (主) is the owner and host (主人).
  composite_memory_hook_es: La persona (人) que sostiene la llama principal de autoridad en el hogar (主) es el amo o anfitrión (主人).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In Chinese social philosophy, 主 (host) and 宾 (guest) define fundamental ritual dynamics. In civic consciousness, the people are celebrated as the true masters of the nation.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dipping 3rd tone followed by rising 2nd tone: zhǔ rén (214-35). 'zhǔ' dips low before ascending into 'rén'.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    王 | wáng | king | Lacks the upper flame dot 丶 of 主
    玉 | yù | jade | Has dot at lower right of 王, not at the top
    入 | rù | enter | Right stroke overlaps left, whereas in 人 left stroke begins at top
    八 | bā | eight | The two strokes do not touch at the apex
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    主要 | zhǔ yào | main; primary
    主动 | zhǔ dòng | active; initiative
    人类 | rén lèi | humanity; mankind
    人事 | rén shì | personnel; human affairs

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 主人 denotes a person possessing ownership, managerial primacy, or host obligations toward guests/employees.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 主人 vs. 东道主 | dōngdàozhǔ | 主人 is general and personal, whereas 东道主 specifically designates the host nation, city, or organizing body of major conferences or competitions.
    2 | 主人 vs. 房东 | fángdōng | 主人 refers to the general proprietor or host, while 房东 is strictly a business-legal term for the landlord leasing property to tenants.
    3 | 主人 vs. 领导 | lǐngdǎo | 主人 indicates ownership or hospitality, whereas 领导 refers to a managerial supervisor or political director exercising hierarchical command.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 大户人家的主人起初并不相信这位衣衫褴褛的年轻人能吃苦。然而几天下来，见子路老实本分、干活毫不懈怠，主人深受感动，不仅按时发给工钱，还在临别时赠予奖金与白米。 | Dàhù rénjiā de zhǔrén qǐchū bìng bù xiāngxìn zhè wèi yīshān-lánlǚ de niánqīngrén néng chīkǔ. Rán'ér jǐ tiān xiàlái, jiàn Zǐlù lǎoshi běnfèn, gànhuó háobù xièdài, zhǔrén shēnshòu gǎndòng, bùjǐn ànshí fā gěi gōngqián, hái zài línbié shí zèngyǔ jiǎngjīn yǔ báimǐ. | The master of the wealthy household initially doubted this ragged youth could bear hardship. But after days of witnessing Zilu's honest and tireless work, the master was moved, paying full wages and rewarding him with extra silver and rice. | El dueño de la rica mansión dudaba al principio de que aquel joven andrajoso soportara la faena. Mas al verlo trabajar con lealtad y sin desmayo, conmovido, le pagó su jornal completo y le obsequió plata y arroz.
  #2 | 在社会学理论中，“主人意识”代表着个体对社群公共事务的高度自觉与责任感。当每一个公民都从被动的旁观者转变为积极的参与者，将自己视为社区与国家的主人时，整个社会的民主治理与文明发展才能获得持久的生命力。 | Zài shèhuìxué lǐlùn zhōng, "zhǔrén yìshí" dàibiǎo zhe gètǐ duì shèqún gōnggòng shìwù de gāodù zìjué yǔ zérèngǎn. Dāng měi yí gè gōngmín dōu cóng bèidòng de pángguānzhě zhuǎnbiàn wéi jījí de cānyùzhě, jiāng zìjǐ shìwéi shèqū yǔ guójiā de zhǔrén shí, zhěnggè shèhuì de mínzhǔ zhìlǐ yǔ wénmíng fāzhǎn cáinéng huòdé chíjiǔ de shēngmìnglì. | In sociological theory, "master consciousness" represents proactive civic civic responsibility. When citizens transform from passive spectators into engaged participants viewing themselves as true masters of community and country, democratic governance flourishes. | En sociología, la conciencia de dueño refleja el compromiso cívico activo. Cuando cada ciudadano deja de ser espectador para verse como protagonista y dueño del destino común, la gobernanza y la civilización cobran una fuerza perdurable.
